            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Is there any downside to downgrading ?\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/webui-vue/commit/063a8e0efc946b319300c610a3fb44dde4433d31 moved us to 6.0"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "No.  The main cost is staying on deprecated, older packages until the CSP conflict with bmcweb is resolved another way.\n\nWe lose access to modern v6 addons (clipboard, unicode-graphemes, etc.).\n\nFor current SOL scope that\u2019s acceptable; it would matter only if we planned richer terminal features later."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "CSP error eliminated - no more runtime style injection violations\nTerminal UI working - renders correctly with xterm v4.19.0\nF12 console clean - no errors or CSP warnings\n\nworking fine +1"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "On click of SOL console in Overview page, not redirected to SOL console page, instead the route I see is `https://localhost:8000/#/*`.\nAnybody else with similar observation?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aravinth Sri Krishna Raja Raghavan",
                        "email": "aravinths@ami.com",
                        "username": "aravinths1"
                    },
                    "message": "for me after clciking SOL console in Overview page it redirected to SOL page only\n\"https://localhost:8000/#/operations/serial-over-lan\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "Oh Okay, Thanks for checking! Is it only for me that this issue is occurring?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nishant Tiwari",
                        "email": "tiwari.nishant@ibm.com",
                        "username": "tiwari-nishant"
                    },
                    "message": "Even I am being routed to this `https://localhost:8000/#/*` upon clicking SOL Console from the overview page"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jason Westover",
                        "email": "jwestover@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "j-westover"
                    },
                    "message": "This MR does not change routing.\n`/#/*` means the route guard denied access (admin-only route).\nAre you hitting this with a Session that has a non-Administrator role?  If so, there is already a MR that would fix that and need not be addressed here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nikhil Ashoka",
                        "email": "a.nikhil@ibm.com",
                        "username": "Nikhil-Ashoka"
                    },
                    "message": "+1, Working with admin user. Also checked with https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/webui-vue/+/90453... Here, it has been handled."
                }
            ],
